---
import '../styles/global.css';

const projectModules = import.meta.glob('../../../projects/*/project.json', { eager: true, import: 'default' });
const projects = Object.values(projectModules).sort((a, b) => a.name.localeCompare(b.name));
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const supportLabels = {
  independent: 'Independent',
  'maintainer-reviewed': 'Maintainer reviewed',
  official: 'Official support',
};
const validationLabels = {
  prototype: 'Prototype',
  'settings-parity': 'Settings parity',
  'build-tested': 'Build tested',
  'science-validated': 'Science validated',
};
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#081b23" />
    <meta name="description" content="One parameter layer for many scientific codes. Discover DIPL integrations, their support status, and the evidence behind them." />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href={base + '/favicon.svg'} />
    <title>SNT Hub — One parameter layer. Many scientific codes.</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="site-header shell">
      <a class="logo" href={base} aria-label="SNT Hub home"><span class="logo-glyph" aria-hidden="true">✳</span><span>SNT<span class="logo-light">/hub</span></span></a>
      <nav aria-label="Main navigation">
        <a href="#how-it-works">How it works</a>
        <a href="#registry">Registry</a>
        <a href="https://scinumtools.github.io/snt3/initiative.html">Initiative <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </nav>
      <a class="header-link" href="https://github.com/scinumtools/snt-hub">View on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
    </header>

    <main>
      <section class="hero shell" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <div class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> AN OPEN SCIENTIFIC SOFTWARE INITIATIVE</div>
          <h1 id="hero-title">One parameter layer.<br /><span>Many scientific codes.</span></h1>
          <p class="hero-lead">A common way to describe, validate, and share simulation inputs, while every code keeps its native format and workflow.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions">
            <a class="button button-bright" href="#registry">Explore the registry <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
            <a class="quiet-link" href="#how-it-works">See how it works <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
          </div>
          <div class="hero-meta"><span><i></i> Open source</span><span><i></i> Optional integration</span><span><i></i> Evidence led</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-visual" aria-label="DIPL model flows through validation and an adapter to native inputs">
          <div class="orbit orbit-one"></div><div class="orbit orbit-two"></div>
          <div class="spark spark-one">✦</div><div class="spark spark-two">✧</div>
          <div class="visual-card input-card"><div class="card-top"><span class="three-dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span><span>model.dip</span></div><pre><span class="code-green">simulation</span>
  box_size <span class="code-blue">float</span> = <span class="code-lime">2.5 m</span>
    <span class="code-muted">!condition</span> (&#123;.&#125; &gt; 0 m)
  steps <span class="code-blue">int</span> = 128</pre></div>
          <div class="visual-connector"><span>typed · checked · translated</span><b aria-hidden="true">→</b></div>
          <div class="visual-card output-card"><div class="card-top"><span class="file-mark">↗</span><span>native input</span></div><pre>BoxSize   <span>2.5</span>
MaxSteps  <span>128</span>
...</pre><div class="output-foot"><span class="ok-dot"></span> Ready for the solver</div></div>
          <div class="visual-stamp">DIPL <span>→</span> SNT <span>→</span> CODE</div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="ticker" aria-label="Initiative principles"><div class="ticker-inner"><span>SEMANTIC INPUTS</span><b>✳</b><span>PHYSICAL UNITS</span><b>✳</b><span>VALIDATION</span><b>✳</b><span>NATIVE OUTPUTS</span><b>✳</b><span>REPRODUCIBILITY</span></div></div>

      <section class="how shell" id="how-it-works" aria-labelledby="how-title">
        <div class="section-title"><div><div class="eyebrow dark"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> THE PRACTICAL IDEA</div><h2 id="how-title">A better interface<br />to existing codes.</h2></div><p>Start with the code you trust. Add a readable parameter model and an adapter that generates the files it already accepts.</p></div>
        <div class="steps">
          <div class="step"><div class="step-number">01 / MODEL</div><div class="step-symbol">&#123; &#125;</div><h3>Describe the science</h3><p>DIPL keeps values, units, types, relationships, and constraints together in a portable definition.</p></div>
          <div class="step"><div class="step-number">02 / CHECK</div><div class="step-symbol">✓</div><h3>Make inputs inspectable</h3><p>SNT evaluates the model and catches declared errors before the settings reach a solver.</p></div>
          <div class="step"><div class="step-number">03 / RUN</div><div class="step-symbol">↗</div><h3>Keep the native workflow</h3><p>A code-specific adapter writes familiar inputs. The solver and its ownership stay with the code.</p></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="registry-section" id="registry" aria-labelledby="registry-title"><div class="shell">
        <div class="registry-heading"><div><div class="eyebrow dark"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> THE REGISTRY</div><h2 id="registry-title">Explore integrations<span class="heading-dot">.</span></h2><p>Every listing says what exists, who supports it, and what has actually been checked.</p></div><div class="registry-total"><strong>{String(projects.length).padStart(2, '0')}</strong><span>{projects.length === 1 ? 'PROJECT' : 'PROJECTS'} LISTED</span></div></div>
        <div class="project-grid">
          {projects.map((project) => <article class="project-card">
            <div class="project-card-top"><span class="project-initials">{project.name.slice(0, 2).toUpperCase()}</span><span class="project-number">PROJECT / {project.id.toUpperCase()}</span></div>
            <h3>{project.name}</h3><p class="project-summary">{project.summary}</p>
            <div class="badge-row"><span class="badge support">{supportLabels[project.support] ?? project.support}</span><span class="badge validation">{validationLabels[project.validation] ?? project.validation}</span></div>
            <p class="validation-note">{project.validation_qualifier}</p>
            <div class="project-scope"><span>INTEGRATION SCOPE</span><p>{project.scope}</p></div>
            <details class="evidence"><summary>Evidence &amp; limitations <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></summary><div class="evidence-body"><p>{project.validation_qualifier}</p><p>{project.limitations}</p><ul>{project.evidence.map((item) => <li><a href={item.url}>{item.label} ↗</a></li>)}</ul></div></details>
            <div class="project-links"><a class="project-main-link" href={project.adapter_url}>DIPL integration <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="project-main-link" href={project.source_url}>Original code <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
          </article>)}
          <div class="invite-card"><span class="invite-mark" aria-hidden="true">✳</span><p class="invite-overline">YOUR CODE COULD BE NEXT</p><h3>Build the next<br />bridge.</h3><p>Help describe an established code’s inputs or review an adapter for your project.</p><a href="https://github.com/scinumtools/snt-hub/issues">Start a conversation <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
        </div>
        <p class="registry-footnote"><strong>About these statuses</strong> Support and validation are independent. “Settings parity” describes a comparison of generated native settings for a stated scope; it does not certify scientific results. <a href="https://github.com/scinumtools/snt-hub/blob/main/PROPOSAL/PROPOSAL.md">Read the status criteria ↗</a></p>
      </div></section>

      <section class="closing shell"><div class="closing-star" aria-hidden="true">✳</div><div><div class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-line"></span> JOIN THE INITIATIVE</div><h2>Better inputs.<br /><span>Stronger science.</span></h2><p>Share a code, review a model, or contribute evidence. The registry grows with every well-described integration.</p><a class="button button-bright" href="https://github.com/scinumtools/snt-hub/issues">Get involved <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
    </main>
    <footer class="site-footer shell"><a class="logo" href={base}><span class="logo-glyph" aria-hidden="true">✳</span><span>SNT<span class="logo-light">/hub</span></span></a><span>One parameter layer. Many scientific codes.</span><div><a href="https://scinumtools.github.io/snt3/">SciNumTools ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/scinumtools/snt-hub">GitHub ↗</a></div></footer>
  </body>
</html>
